### Solution:
```rust
fn extract_endpoint(url: &str) -> Option<String> {
    if let Some(index) = url.rfind('/') {
        if index < url.len() - 1 {
            Some(url[index + 1..].to_string())
        } else {
            Some("".to_string())
        }
    } else {
        None
    }
}
```
In this solution, we use the `rfind` method to find the last occurrence of the forward slash in the URL. If a forward slash is found, we extract the substring after it and return it as Some(endpoint). If the URL ends with a forward slash, we return Some("") as the endpoint. If no forward slash is found, we return None.

