```csharp
public static async Task<ReservationDetails> GetReservationDetailsAsync(this IReservationsDetailsOperations operations, string reservationId, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default(CancellationToken))
{
    if (operations == null)
    {
        throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(operations), "Operations cannot be null.");
    }

    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(reservationId))
    {
        throw new ArgumentException("Reservation ID cannot be null or empty.", nameof(reservationId));
    }

    try
    {
        // Call the API endpoint to retrieve reservation details asynchronously
        ReservationDetails reservationDetails = await operations.GetReservationDetailsWithHttpMessagesAsync(reservationId, null, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);

        return reservationDetails;
    }
    catch (HttpOperationException ex)
    {
        // Handle HTTP operation exceptions
        throw new Exception("Failed to retrieve reservation details. HTTP operation exception occurred.", ex);
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        // Handle other exceptions
        throw new Exception("Failed to retrieve reservation details. An exception occurred.", ex);
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `GetReservationDetailsAsync` method is implemented to perform input validation, call the API endpoint using the `operations` parameter, and handle exceptions appropriately. The method returns a `Task<ReservationDetails>` containing the retrieved reservation details. Additionally, it supports asynchronous programming and cancellation using the provided `cancellationToken`.

